      "content": "Definition: Understandability refers to how easily developers can comprehend and maintain the test code.\n\nTask: Improve the understandability of the test `JsonTypeInfoTest_testMutators.java` (path:- /Users/tenghaha/Projects/New_Agent_understandability_improvement/data/original/jackson-annotations/manual/testcases/JsonTypeInfoTest/JsonTypeInfoTest_testMutators.java). The refactored code must be syntactically correct and compilable against the provided CUT signatures. Do not alter the runtime behaviour of the original test: the same methods must be called with the same arguments and produce the same expected outcomes.\n"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Let me check the `AnnotationTestUtil` base class to find the `Anno1` annotation.Now let me check the compile setup in my working directory.Now I have everything I need. Let me write the improved test with better understandability — clearer variable names, logical grouping with comments, and the required `Anno1` nested class.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored `JsonTypeInfoTest_testMutators.java` adds the required `Anno1` nested class with an explanatory comment, renames the reused `v2`/`v3` variables to descriptive names (`withMinimalClass`, `withSimpleName`, `withExternalProperty`, `withStringImpl`), and groups assertions under clearly labeled sections (`withIdType`, `withInclusionType`, `withDefaultImpl`, `withIdVisible`, `withPropertyName`) with brief comments explaining the \"why\" behind each `assertSame` identity check."
    }
